{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThere are a lot of things which could be cut\u00a0\u2014 trees, paper, \"the rope\". In this problem you are going to cut a sequence of integers.There is a sequence of integers, which contains the equal number of even and odd numbers. Given a limited budget, you need to make maximum possible number of cuts such that each resulting segment will have the same number of odd and even integers.Cuts separate a sequence to continuous (contiguous) segments. You may think about each cut as a break between two adjacent elements in a sequence. So after cutting each element belongs to exactly one segment. Say, $$$[4, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 4, 4, 5, 5]$$$ $$$\\to$$$ two cuts $$$\\to$$$ $$$[4, 1 | 2, 3, 4, 5 | 4, 4, 5, 5]$$$. On each segment the number of even elements should be equal to the number of odd elements.The cost of the cut between $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ numbers is $$$|x - y|$$$ bitcoins. Find the maximum possible number of cuts that can be made while spending no more than $$$B$$$ bitcoins.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int btcAmount = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] btcCosts = new int[100];\n        int evenCount = 0, oddCount = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int left = sc.nextInt();\n            if ((left & 1) == 0) evenCount++;\n            else oddCount++;\n            if (evenCount == oddCount && i != n - 1) {\n                int right = sc.nextInt();\n                i++;\n                int btcCost = Math.abs(left - right);\n                btcCosts[btcCost]++;\n                evenCount = 0;\n                oddCount = 0;\n            }\n        }\n        int sawedAmount = 0;\n        int currentBTCCost = 0;\n        for (int cost = 0; cost < 100; cost++) {\n            int count = btcCosts[cost];\n            while (count-- > 0) {\n                currentBTCCost += cost;\n                if (currentBTCCost <= btcAmount) {\n                    sawedAmount++;\n                } else {\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(sawedAmount);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int btcAmount = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] costs = new int[n]; // Store valid cut costs\n        int count = 0; // Number of valid cuts\n        \n        int evenCount = 0, oddCount = 0;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int num = sc.nextInt();\n            if ((num & 1) == 0) {\n                evenCount++;\n            } else {\n                oddCount++;\n            }\n            \n            // When we have equal even and odd counts and not at the end\n            if (evenCount == oddCount && evenCount > 0 && i != n - 1) {\n                // Read the next element to calculate the cost\n                int nextNum = sc.nextInt();\n                int cost = Math.abs(num - nextNum);\n                costs[count++] = cost;\n                \n                // Reset counters for the next segment\n                evenCount = 0;\n                oddCount = 0;\n                \n                // Skip the next element since we already processed it\n                i++;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Sort the costs to prioritize cheaper cuts\n        java.util.Arrays.sort(costs, 0, count);\n        \n        // Greedily select cuts within budget\n        int maxCuts = 0;\n        int currentCost = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n            if (currentCost + costs[i] <= btcAmount) {\n                currentCost += costs[i];\n                maxCuts++;\n            } else {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(maxCuts);\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.407998726994265e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -7.748573807475623e-06, -1.9430925021879375e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.18120616674423218, -0.20141859352588654, -5.245195097813848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.629365427419543e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -9.775113539944869e-06, -7.390948667307384e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.0847986231965479e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.1219027985353023e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -5.722029527532868e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -